  /// stored, a restart treats every collection as read. To read a collection again, send
  /// a `snapshot-execute` signal. Unlike `postgres_cdc`, a new key does not cause a new
  /// read. The reads a signal requests store their progress here too, whether or not
  /// `enabled` is set. While `enabled` is `false` and no `signal_collection_name` is set,
  /// nothing keeps the progress current, so the input discards what is left under this
  /// key and enabling either later never resumes a read the stream has long since moved
  /// past.
  checkpoint_cache_key: String?

  /// How long the snapshot waits before retrying a chunk read that failed transiently,
